File Index

/areas.test.ts
Purpose: Route tests both gate states: listing/preview/diff/download, script + dangling-vnum 400s, atomic save with backup, reload signals, new-area creation (area.lst registration, overlap 400, duplicate 409), header range guards (shrink/overlap 400s, rename saves), Phase 11 conditional saves (baseHash 409 with disk untouched) and world-index ref resolution with live cache invalidation.

/areas.ts
Purpose: Area REST API — list/get(+baseHash)/preview(diff+scripts+refs incl. resolved external links)/download/save plus POST /api/areas new-area creation (copyover-flagged); optional baseHash makes PUT conditional (409 {error,currentHash}); scripts + vnum-ref + header-range validation 400s before disk; no error escapes a handler.

/audit-view.test.ts
Purpose: GET /api/audit tests via full registerRoutes: empty-before-any-mutation, anonymous 401 / API-key 403, newest-first order + ?limit, unparseable line degrades to { raw }.

/audit-view.ts
Purpose: GET /api/audit (Phase 10) — master-only, read-only tail of backups/audit.log (newest first, default 100 / cap 500); missing file = empty, bad line = { raw }; never truncates the log. Takes an introspectConfig param passed straight through to requireMaster (2026-07-24) so an account actor gets the same 403-not-401 treatment here as under /api/auth.

/auth.test.ts
Purpose: Guard + lifecycle tests via full registerRoutes: first-run key gen, 401/403 matrix, create→use→rotate→revoke, master rotation, per-install uniqueness, guard-off mode, corrupt-file lockdown, audit lines without secrets. Phase 4 block: introspect fallback against a fake auth-server (local-first no-network-call proof, unconfigured no-op, valid/invalid/unreachable/hanging/bad-key-path cases, plus a regression case proving requireMaster/GET /api/auth/keys also falls back — an account actor gets 403 not 401).

/auth.ts
Purpose: Phase 9 access guard — authGuard middleware (non-GET /api/* requires a valid bearer) + master-only /api/auth key-management routes (list/create/rotate/revoke, rotate-master); plaintext tokens only in create/rotate responses; exports requireMaster for the audit viewer. Phase 2 (centralized auth service) adds GET /api/auth/introspect-check?token=... — additive proof that a real /api/introspect call against auth-server works, reusing this same master-only mount rather than a new guard. Phase 4: authGuard falls back to introspect() (bounded ~3s timeout) for any token the local store misses, producing a BuilderActor{kind:'account'} — local-store tokens are checked first and never touch the network. requireMaster now takes the SAME introspectConfig and falls back too (2026-07-24 fix): before, an introspection-valid account actor landed in requireMaster's bare 401 bucket instead of the 403 "not master" bucket, which mud-builder-client's AccessPage status probe (GET /api/auth/keys) reads as "token REJECTED" even though the key worked everywhere else.

/codegen.test.ts
Purpose: /api/codegen tests: empty GET on missing file, 401 write gate, 400 invalid spec + stock-name collision, save emits an audit line, 409 stale baseHash, text/plain patch download content, unknown-funName 404.

/codegen.ts
Purpose: New-spell codegen API (Phase 14a) — GET /api/codegen/spells (open, {specs, baseHash}), gated+audited PUT (every spec re-validated via validateSpellSpec against stock + live skills.dat overlay names, 400 on any error), GET /api/codegen/spells/:funName/patch (open, regenerates the 4-section C patchText on the fly as text/plain, 404 unknown). Specs are builder metadata only — the game never reads spells.json; deployment stays human.

/groups.test.ts
Purpose: /api/groups tests both gating modes: stock fallback GET (27 groups), preview text + cycle 400, 403 when writes disabled, PUT/backup/DELETE round trip, unknown-member 400, corrupt-overlay fallback with parseError, Phase 12 baseHash matrix (null first save, stale 409 disk untouched, fresh, legacy).

/groups.ts
Purpose: groups.dat REST API (Phase 8) — GET (overlay or stock fallback, +baseHash) , POST preview, gated PUT (optional baseHash → conditional, 409 carries currentHash) with copyover note, DELETE (revert to compiled table); same never-crash safe() contract as areas/skills.

/import.test.ts
Purpose: .are import tests both gate states: clean preview (no writes) + commit (byte-identical disk, area.lst registration, copyover flag), broken/overlap 400s with zero writes, overwrite 409-then-backup, >1mb body via the scoped parser, oversized/binary/traversal store guards.

/import.ts
Purpose: .are import API (Phase 10) — POST /api/import/area/preview (quarantine report, never writes) + gated PUT /api/import/area commit; scoped 2mb JSON parser registered before the app-wide 1mb one.

/map.test.ts
Purpose: /api/map tests: single-area shape with internal/external/dangling exits told apart (external carries file+name), 404 unlisted / 400 invalid name, world aggregation of areas + directional links with a broken file tolerated.

/map.ts
Purpose: Read-only map aggregates (Phase 12) — GET /api/map/:file (rooms+exits with locks, cross-area targets resolved via worldVnumIndex to {file,name}, Phase 12b `warps` from R-script `warp <vnum>` lines) and GET /api/map (world graph: area nodes + directional cross-area exit links with per-exit detail); never writes, never audited, unparseable files listed with parseError.

/presence.test.ts
Purpose: Presence tests: registry unit (heartbeat/list/refresh, lazy TTL expiry via injected clock), standalone routes (anonymous heartbeat, 400 guards), full-app auth-on (401 anon, credential-named entry, open GET, never audited). Phase 4 case: a centrally-issued token heartbeats under its auth-server label via the same fake-introspect pattern as auth.test.ts.

/presence.ts
Purpose: Advisory presence routes (Phase 11): guarded POST /api/presence heartbeat (name from the acting credential, returned to the caller) + open GET listing live entries; scoped 4kb parser; excluded from auditing.

/reload.ts
Purpose: POST /api/reload — writes the hot (reload.signal, per-file) or copyover (copyover.signal) sentinel the game polls; write-gated.

/spawn.test.ts
Purpose: GET /api/areas/:file/spawn tests: an M/E/G-style chain (guard wielding a local sword) plus a cross-area P (a local chest holding an object whose template is only defined in a neighbor area) proving the real worldVnumIndex resolver is wired in, not just a local lookup; a broken neighbor file in area.lst doesn't break a healthy file's spawn preview; requesting spawn for the broken file itself 400s (parse error) rather than 500ing; 404/400 filename guards.

/spawn.ts
Purpose: Read-only spawn preview (Phase 13) — GET /api/areas/:file/spawn runs merc-area's simulateResets over the parsed on-disk model with worldVnumIndex wired as the cross-area resolver; mirrors routes/areas.ts's `safe()` error taxonomy (AreaStoreError→its status, ParseError→400, else 500) rather than map.ts's simpler one, since a parse failure must 400 here.

/skills.test.ts
Purpose: /api/skills tests both gating modes: stock fallback GET, preview text + validation 400s, 403 when writes disabled, PUT/backup/DELETE round trip, unproven-pair 400, corrupt-overlay fallback with parseError, Phase 12 baseHash matrix (null first save, stale 409 disk untouched, fresh/wrong/legacy/400).

/skills.ts
Purpose: skills.dat REST API (Phase 7) — GET (overlay or stock fallback, +baseHash), POST preview, gated PUT (optional baseHash → conditional, 409 carries currentHash; exports readBaseHash shared with groups) with copyover note, DELETE (revert to compiled table); same never-crash safe() contract as areas.

/world.test.ts
Purpose: /api/world aggregation tests: counts, cross-area warning, and a listed-but-broken file reported instead of dropped.

/world.ts
Purpose: GET /api/world — read-only aggregate over every area.lst entry (header, entity counts, resolver-backed refs: errors, proven-INVALID warnings, resolved external links) plus Phase 12b limitPressure (world-wide spawn demand per mob/object vs the tightest reset limit, db.c decoding, flagged on the defining area); unparseable files stay listed with their parse error.
